Well, I've done it! My level 13 priest ascended after the most challenging
and exciting game I have ever played: I played the entire game without ANY
weapons ! Just kicking monsters around, running away or bashing the
occasional swallowing monsters with my gloved hands because I didn't have
enough room inside the monster to kick properly. I had a pick-axe which I
used only for digging and a unicorn horn which I used only for healing.
Wow! What a game! I used a wand of death to dispose of the Wizard.
I couldn't have done it without Siphyllis, my former-house-cat-turned-
green-dragon who saw me safely through the first 13 levels, killing
all shopkeepers (and unfortunately two temple priests to my god...), as
well as a bunch of monsters that I promptly ate to gain useful intrinsics.
Unfortunately, on level 13 Siphyllis trap-polymorphed into a trapper and
subsequently disappeared (into the ceiling?), hiding for a monster to
attack by surprise; I couldn't make it come out again... In all, I 
encountered 2 shops (one of them a weapons store: useless to me!) and
2 temples to my god, with about 6 altars total and three sinks (plus
one ghost of mine without much of interest).

I finished the game with: +3 shield of reflection, +3 Hawaiian shirt,
+2 helm of telepathy, +0 speed boots, +0 cloak of magic resistance,
+0 gauntlets of power and blessed +4 black dragon scale mail (for a
resulting armor class of -23). Before ascending, I dropped everything
to achieve the lowest possible score, so that I finished with the stats:
ST: 18/04   DX: 15  CO: 16  IN: 10  WI: 17  CH: 12
HP: 80 (80)  PW: 76  AC: 4    level: 13  gold: 0

I ascended after 31552 moves, WITH A TOTAL OF 340904 POINTS !!! Has
anybody ascended with a lower score???

By the way, I almost didn't make it. On the endgame, the Wizard cornered me
when I had 0 death charges left. He double-troubled me, and called on
some pets to help (an Umber Hulk and an Invisible Stalker). Fortunately
I had a ring of conflict, so the Wizard's pets turned against him, and
as I was kicking along he killed me once (I had an amulet of life saving),
and his Vampire Lord alter ego brought me down to 25 HP before being bitten
to death by the Stalker. Whew, that was close... About 20 steps away from
my god's altar!!!



Lastly, and on a different chain of thought, has anyone ever noticed the
striking similarities between the Nethack Gods and the Dons of Organized
Crime?
- favors and protection can be obtained by dealing with appropriate
  intermediaries, at exorbitant prices...
- you REALLY don't want to make any of them angry at you...
- once you've pledged allegiance, you can get into serious trouble by
  approaching rivals...
- proper offerings can sometimes restore an amiable relationship gone sour...
- there are realms where their influence is diminished...
- violence and kick-ass weapons are all-pervasive in dealing with them...
I'm sure more comparisons can be made, and I invite them!

